# Grocery Store Management API

REST API for managing a small grocery store: products and stock, customers with credit, sales and customer payments. Built for a real grocery store.

**Live demo:  https://grocery-store-management-angular.vercel.app/**  · **Frontend repo:https://github.com/KevinCHSE/GroceryStoreManagement-Spring**
> the project runs on Render's free tier, the first request can take up to a minute to wake the server.

## Features
- Product catalog with images and stock control
- Customers with credit tracking: used credit grows with credit sales and drops with payments
- Invoices paid in cash or on credit; stock and balances update in the same transaction
- Payments (abonos) and per-customer payment reports
- JWT login with roles (`ADMIN`, `USER`) and user management

## Tech stack
Java 26 · Spring Boot 4 · Spring Security + JWT · Spring Data JPA / Hibernate · MySQL · Bean Validation · Maven · Docker · Render

## Architecture
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Angular SPA] -->|REST + JWT| B[Controllers]
    B --> C[Services - business rules]
    C --> D[Repositories - Spring Data JPA]
    D --> E[(MySQL)]
```

## Technical highlights
- Layered architecture (controller / service / repository) with DTOs and request validation
- Stateless authentication with JWT, BCrypt password hashing and role-based authorization
- Business operations wrapped in `@Transactional` so stock and customer balances stay consistent
- Centralized error handling with `@RestControllerAdvice`
- Secrets loaded from environment variables, never committed
- Dockerized and deployed on Render

## Run locally
**Requirements:** JDK 26, MySQL 8

```bash
git clone https://github.com/KevinCHSE/GroceryStoreManagement-Spring.git 
cd grocery-store-management-spring
cp .env.example .env     # then edit the values
./mvnw spring-boot:run
```
The API runs at `http://localhost:8080`. 

this porject was designed as a private API, sso creating the first user requires a
temporary change:
1. In `UserController`, remove `@PreAuthorize` from `saveUser`.
2. In `filterChain`, add `.requestMatchers(HttpMethod.POST, "/User/saveUser").permitAll()`.
3. Start the app and send `POST http://localhost:8080/User/saveUser` from Postman:
   { "id": "123456789", "name": "yourName", "password": "change-me",
     "phone": "8888-8888", "enable": true, "Admin": true }
4. **Revert both changes**, otherwise anyone can create admin users.

## API overview
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/login` | Get a JWT |
| GET | `/apiClients/getClients` | List customers |
| GET | `/apiPayment/getPaymentReports/{id}` | Payment report for a customer |
| GET | `/apiImage/{id}/image` | Product image |

